# who may enter the velvet room.
#
# name:password:uid:description
#
# these passwords are in plain text, and that is not an oversight to be
# fixed later -- it is the honest shape of what this demonstrates. the
# interesting part of a user is not how its password is stored but what
# its uid can and cannot reach, and that part is enforced by hardware:
# ring 3, an address space of its own, and a kernel that checks before
# it hands anything over. storing these properly needs somewhere to
# write, which is what a real disk is for.
#
# uid 0 is the master of the velvet room. everyone else is a guest.

igor:velvet:0:master of the velvet room
elizabeth:margaret:0:its attendant
guest:guest:1000:a visitor, and treated as one
